WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.470
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.380
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:21.130
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.830
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.930
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.300
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.230
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.480
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.750
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:03.490
What is truly precious?

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:13.000
Saint Fire Giga!

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.080
Yugi, you're forgetting something important.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:17.790
What?

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:20.550
What can be seen but remains unseen?

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.180
Yugi, do you know the answer?

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.400
The Legendary Strongest Warrior
Black Luster Soldier Descends

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:43.380
As long as she has Shadow of Eyes, I can't place my monsters in defense position.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:48.860
But if I attack, Mirror Wall will cut my monsters' attack points in half.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.260
What should I do?

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.080
Wonderful.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.890
Her Harpie deck has no weaknesses.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.680
Confusion is growing in Yugi's heart.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.300
I know the feeling of defeat is spreading inside you.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.310
What's wrong with Yugi?

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:12.940
Mai is much stronger than the times she dueled Jonouchi and me.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.660
So this is Mai's true skills.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.380
Was it luck that I defeated her before?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:23.290
No, Jonouchi.  Defeating me wasn't luck.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.690
Those were my skills at that time.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:32.300
To be honest, I felt disgraced when I lost to Jonouchi.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:42.560
I couldn't face the fact that I lost, but I couldn't ignore the voice in my heart.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:47.300
It's what can be seen but remains unseen.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:52.480
When I finally faced my true self, I understood what those words meant.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.650
Your true self?

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:00.390
Jonouchi, do you know why you survived Duelist Kingdom?

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.180
Of course I do!

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.580
It's because my friends supported me!

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.870
Without them, a guy who finished 8th in the regionals couldn't have gotten this far!

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.480
Jonouchi knows that he's weak.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.680
He tries to become stronger to overcome his weakness.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.910
That's the courage of a duelist!

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:24.680
That's what I learned from Jonouchi!

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.150
From me?

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:32.020
Yugi, a duelist's courage isn't tested after a victory.  It's tested after a loss!

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:38.030
And you can't have true courage unless you're prepared to lose and get hurt.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.460
Yugi, do you have such courage?

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:45.170
Prepared to lose and get hurt...

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.670
I see!  Back then...

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:54.560
When Kaiba was willing to risk his life, I feared losing.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.950
I feared losing and hurting my pride.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:03.550
But when I lost the duel, the one who was hurt instead of me...

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:07.830
The one who stood between me and Kaiba and actually suffered was...

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.430
My other self.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:14.200
I never realized that.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:23.440
Actually, I didn't want to see that my other self's strength compensated for my weaknesses.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.560
That's what can be seen but remains unseen!

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.320
Mai!

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:35.420
I'm proud to have met you.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:38.620
And now the real battle begins!

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.400
It's too late.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.260
Even you can't turn this situation around.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.880
My turn!

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.270
I'm no longer afraid of losing!

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.010
Brain Control!

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.850
Brain Control?

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:08.400
Yes.  I can brainwash your monster and control it for one turn.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:12.920
I use this card to brainwash Harpie's Pet Dragon.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.160
Too bad, but Pet Dragon is Harpie's servant.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:27.000
Even if you brainwash it, it won't attack Harpie.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.470
I know that.  I won't attack your Harpie.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.210
I set one card and...

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.620
Catapult Turtle!

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:41.720
I place Harpie's Pet Dragon on Catapult in attack position!

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:50.490
Since it's in attack position, Mirror Wall appears.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:54.000
Harpie's Pet Dragon is ready to launch!

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:55.760
Oh no.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.740
Catapult Turtle has the ability to destroy walls and fortresses.

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:00.740
Here I go!

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:06.680
You did it!

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.550
My Mirror Wall...

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:11.920
It's not just your Mirror Wall.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:17.280
The monster that Catapult Turtle tributed was yours.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:24.460
So you lose half of Harpie's Pet Dragon's 2300 attack points, which is 1150 life points.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:29.080
All right, Yugi!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.830
It's time to turn the tables!

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.640
Yugi boy's mind is overflowing with fighting spirit.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.170
What could have caused this?

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:46.180
Mai and my other self made me realize that a duelist gains true strength when he's ready for the worst.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.000
It's my turn.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.860
The only monster on Yugi's field is Catapult Turtle.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:07:00.240
If Harpie Lady destroys Catapult Turtle, Yugi will have 0 life points, and I'll win.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:04.430
But I'm worried about Yugi's set card.

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:08.800
If it's a trap, I have no card in my hand to deal with it.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.080
What should I do?

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.940
Should I attack or not attack?

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:18.730
Attack me, Mai.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:24.920
I will...

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.060
...not attack.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:33.680
Even if I don't make my move now, I still have the advantage.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:38.630
Instead, I'll use this card to strengthen my Harpies!

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:41.600
Elegant Egotist!

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.320
Harpie Ladies!

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.360
How's that, Yugi?

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.280
I end my turn.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:03.400
But you'll experience my hellish harem next turn!

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:06.960
It's my turn.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.630
Too bad, Mai.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.130
What's so funny?

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:14.520
If you attacked me last turn, I would've lost.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:15.650
What?

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:18.240
My set card is...

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.280
Monster Recovery.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.400
It only lets me exchange cards in my hand.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.680
You missed your chance to win, Mai.

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:34.940
Well done.  But I can win next turn with my Harpie Ladies' Triangle Attack!

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:40.700
Due to Shadow of Eyes, my monsters are forced into attack position.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:44.700
There's nothing I can do with these cards in my hand.  In that case...

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.780
I activate the spell Monster Recovery this turn!

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:54.110
I return my monster and the cards in my hand to the deck and shuffle.

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:57.000
Then I draw five new cards.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:05.350
None of these cards are strong enough to defeat her Harpie Ladies.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:10.120
My Harpie Ladies have 2700 attack points.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:15.930
You can't easily draw a monster with more attack points than them.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:20.530
And due to Shadow of Eyes, you're not allowed to defend.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.600
It's over, Yugi.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:42.660
What's wrong, Yugi?

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.460
You're not the type who would give up!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.720
Yugi, do your best!

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.730
Mai must have a weakness!

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:53.960
But Mai's pheromone card is powerful.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.560
This won't be easy.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.900
Pheromones are nothing!

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:01.540
Yugi, don't let her seduce you!

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:03.760
Wait.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.640
Harpie's Shadow of Eyes...

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:08.120
That's it!  There's something I can do!

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.630
I play this card in defense position!

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:13.030
That's pointless.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:16.800
Shadow of Eyes forces all monsters into attack position!

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:19.630
It's not happening?

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:20.960
Impossible!

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:22.430
I thought so.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.300
I'll tell you what card I played.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:40.350
Shadow of Eyes can tempt men, but it doesn't work on women.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.400
I didn't expect that strategy.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.520
I end my turn!

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:47.890
He did it!  He managed to survive.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:52.720
But he only survived this turn.  He's still on the verge of defeat.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.900
Mystical Elf will soon be destroyed.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.700
You're so stubborn.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.300
But it's over for you.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.540
My turn!

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:07.340
First, I play Monster Reborn to resurrect one monster!

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:09.210
Monster Reborn!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:12.710
That's...

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:15.900
Harpie's Pet Dragon resurrects!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:20.320
It gains 300 attack points for every Harpie Lady on the field!

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:21.500
What?

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.460
2900 attack points?

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:26.160
Now I attack this turn.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:34.170
Harpie Ladies, Triangle Ecstasy Spark!

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.310
Yugi!

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:41.700
Mystical Elf is destroyed!

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:45.610
It's your turn, Yugi.

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:52.500
But there's nothing you can do against my monsters' overwhelming attack power.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:54.190
I win, Yugi!

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.900
The card at the top of my deck...

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:06.270
Everything depends on that one card.

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:09.840
Everyone's fates depend on it!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:15.040
My other self, lend me your strength.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:18.780
Give me the strength to believe in my cards!

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:23.840
No matter how hard you try, defeat awaits you.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.090
Swords of Revealing Light?

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:34.830
He drew Swords of Revealing Light in this difficult situation?

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:38.140
Good!  Mai is sealed away for three turns!

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:40.500
Yugi still has a chance to win!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:45.560
It's pointless to resist, but whatever.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:49.940
This is your last spark as a duelist before you burn yourself out completely.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:52.750
You can have my three turns so that I can watch that happen.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:56.980
Mai, my passion for battle will never burn out.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:03.660
Harpie's Pet Dragon is a powerful monster that gains attack points for every Harpie on the field.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:07.630
Unless I destroy it, there's no way I can win.

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:09.660
So I only have one goal.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:13.170
I must bring out the legendary strongest warrior within three turns.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:17.100
Yugi, there are no monsters on your field!

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:17.900
Yeah.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:22.430
I play this card and end my turn.

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:28.780
What's with that tiny monster?

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:36.020
Even though it's weak, it's eager to attack because of my Harpies' pheromones!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.800
Are you making fun of me, Yugi?

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.720
I'm dead serious, Mai.

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:50.540
Among thousands of cards, I chose this card for my deck because it's an important piece for victory.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:55.900
I'll never understand why you would put such a weak card in your deck.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:14:00.540
While Swords of Revealing Light is active, I can't attack.

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:03.560
I'll draw a card and end my turn.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.020
Yugi, you have two turns left.

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:13.990
I can't bring out the legendary strongest warrior with these cards.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.000
I'm missing the key card.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.470
It's my turn.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.470
No, this isn't the card I need either.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:27.470
I don't know what you're planning to do, but I do know one thing.

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:30.980
The goddess of victory won't smile upon you.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:33.280
In that case, I'll play this card.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.280
Monster Reborn!

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:41.880
I use this card to resurrect Gaia The Fierce Knight.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.560
Gaia The Fierce Knight.

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:48.090
I guess that's better than Kuriboh.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:52.600
But it's nowhere close to Harpie's Pet Dragon's attack points.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.830
I end my turn!

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.360
My turn!

00:14:57.780 --> 00:14:59.340
This isn't what I need either.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:00.440
Yugi...

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.140
He'll be fine, Anzu.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:07.580
Trust him.  The look in Yugi's eyes says that he hasn't given up.

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.380
I see.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:17.760
He intends to bring out the legendary strongest warrior.

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:22.240
But he can't do that without a certain card.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:29.220
Yugi boy, can you draw that card in one last turn?

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.140
My turn!

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:36.540
I did it!  I drew another Harpie card!

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:41.950
If I play this card next turn, I'll have four Harpies on my field.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:46.950
Harpie's Pet Dragon will have 3200 attack points.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:53.460
When Swords of Revealing Light's effect ends next turn, I'll show you my perfect victory.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.160
I end my turn!

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.470
Everything you did during these three turns was pointless.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:18.030
This card is the door of destiny.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:24.620
Am I still afraid?

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:29.960
I...

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:38.570
Everyone!

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:45.540
That's right.  I no longer need to be afraid of losing.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:49.230
Everyone will always be with me.

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:55.140
Will this card close my path or bring me light?

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:56.400
I'll find out!

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:00.160
What?

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:04.340
Yugi boy, you're unbelievable!

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:08.620
Mai.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.070
I've gathered all the pieces for victory!

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:17.360
The spell card Black Luster Ritual!

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:18.840
Black Luster Ritual?

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:28.950
Black Luster Ritual tributes monsters whose combined Levels equal 8.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:37.560
One soul invites light!

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:40.230
Another soul guides darkness!

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:49.300
The souls of light and dark create the light of chaos!

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:56.040
What?

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:00.650
Black Luster Soldier descends!

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:04.590
That's the legendary strongest warrior?

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.330
Black Luster Soldier attacks!

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:09.760
Chaos Blade!

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:18.600
Harpie's Pet Dragon is destroyed!

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.880
My Harpie's Pet Dragon...

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:27.110
Incredible.

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:30.120
Yugi's trump card is the mightiest warrior.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:32.120
Very impressive.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.700
The duel is over.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:47.620
Her fighting spirit is fading from her mind.

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:50.500
I only needed one more turn.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:57.580
If I was able to play this card before Black Luster Soldier appeared, I wouldn't have lost.

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:02.760
There's no card in my deck that can destroy Black Luster Soldier.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.550
That's a surrender card.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:10.800
Mai.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:13.060
What's going on?

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:14.700
It's a surrender card.

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:19.060
Placing your hand on your deck means you're surrendering.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:20.780
Mai...

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:24.820
I don't want to see my Harpies get hurt on the next turn.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.320
I lose, Yugi.

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:31.810
Mai!

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:33.900
Thank you.

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:36.300
Yugi...

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:41.250
Thanks to you, I realized something that I've been overlooking in this duel.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:44.990
Something that can be seen but remains unseen.

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:49.020
There's no such thing as a flawless duelist.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:51.500
Everyone has weaknesses in their hearts.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:56.830
Even though we can see our own weaknesses, we choose to look away.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:00.260
It can be seen but remains unseen.

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:04.510
By looking away, we don't notice these weaknesses in our hearts.

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.960
Yugi, there are two types of defeat.

00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:11.250
Defeat that ends everything and defeat that leads to victory.

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:15.770
I'm confident that this defeat will make me stronger.

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:18.260
And I will achieve my dream in the end!

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:37.850
It's the second match of the tournament finals.

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:40.450
It's finally Jonouchi's turn!

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:43.980
His opponent is the former American champion Bandit Keith.

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:48.780
Since you've come this far, you better win - even if it depends on luck!

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:51.910
What?  You lost your entry card?

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:54.440
What's wrong with you?

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:58.030
